EDMA v1 global OF reference ownership (patch 016)
================================================

Run from the source worktree with a fresh evidence directory:

  /usr/bin/python3 tests/test-edma-of-references.py \
    --upstream-cache /Volumes/FX-MD87/Review-AX6/upstreams/nss/qca-nss-dp \
    --output /Volumes/FX-MD87/Review-AX6/audits/20261030/core-risk-phase2/EDMA-OF016-gcc-r2 \
    --compiler /opt/homebrew/bin/gcc-16

For Clang use --compiler /usr/bin/clang --sanitize and another fresh output.
No make, firmware/target build, hardware, network or archived program is used.

Source and patch binding
------------------------
The runner exports local git pin d8f802f08fd8ff31057ba58edb20bbe448e7b505
twice. It applies current 001-015 to both and 016 only to candidate. Every
patch is checked at its full declared old/new hunk positions by the shared
tests/edma_patch_context.py before patch, then verify_applied checks exact
expected file bytes after patch. INPUTS.json records the helper SHA, every
patch SHA, per-hunk declared coordinates, before/after file SHAs and complete
prepared-tree file SHAs. Patch-tool stdout alone is not an offset oracle.
Final qualification uses the header-maintained 008/012 chain, not old r5
zero-offset claims. Older r5 may retain exact-context behavior evidence only.

Only edma_data_plane.c may differ between prepared trees. After removing the
four authorized changed function bodies, all remaining C tokens must match.
The runner, fixture, README, shared lexer/helper and patch bytes must remain
stable through each run. No shared file is modified by this runner.

Actual definitions extracted and compiled
-----------------------------------------
Complete bodies are extracted unchanged using the unchanged 014 C lexer:

  edma_of_get_pdata, edma_release_of_refs (candidate only), edma_init,
  edma_free_irqs, edma_stop_napi, edma_release_mmio, edma_cleanup_locked,
  edma_cleanup, edma_disable_port, edma_disable_interrupts,
  edma_enable_interrupts, edma_close_member, edma_retire_port, edma_if_open,
  edma_if_close, edma_irq_init, edma_register_netdevice, edma_if_init,
  nss_dp_clear_host_ctx, nss_dp_abort_host_probe.

The original pdata function is NOT stubbed. Complete current arch, register
and EDMA dataplane headers are included with only include directives removed.
Each extracted function's source path, line and SHA are saved in fragments
JSON; generated C and binaries are preserved. There is no source scheduling
insertion. Physical probe/open/close/remove as a whole are not run here.
Extraction/compilation does not mean every listed definition is individually
executed. In particular edma_if_close is compiled but is not invoked by this
fixture; no new direct close-path runtime coverage is claimed from this suite.

Model boundaries
-----------------
Bottom-level OF lookups, property/address reads, reference counters,
reservations, mappings, dummy allocation, IRQ/NAPI/RCU/RTNL and DMA/ring APIs
are host ledger models, not kernel implementations. edma_hw_init and
edma_cleanup_rings are explicit mocks with pdev last-use checks. The 15th
injection models the unpublished hw-init error return; it does not rerun all
013 allocation sites or the real DMA teardown code. It proves ordering at
the called API boundary, not DMA idle, firmware behavior or device release.
External initial node/device counts remain 5 and 7; puts may consume only
the reference acquired by this global EDMA init. CONFIG_OF_DYNAMIC on/off is
modeled separately: logical get/put pairing is checked even when node refs
are physical no-ops. IRQ use includes the actual stored pdev dev_id.

36 positive scenarios cover both node configurations, all 15 init failure
points, a successful failed-init retry after each, a foreign busy region,
node-only/both-ref partial state, live-init rejection, replacement drvdata,
override/repeat override/final/repeat final, and a physical host probe-abort
helper with a live peer. Failed request_mem_region must not release the
foreign reservation. Partial refs must be put even without a mapping.
Override keeps refs/mapping until the final false cleanup. Every put checks
IRQ, ring/DMA, dummy, mapping and reservation retirement and cleared global
reference pointers. Trace output is a modeled API ledger, not an HW trace.

Foreign drvdata protection means final cleanup does not clear drvdata that
has since changed to a foreign value. Successful init STILL unconditionally
sets drvdata to &edma_hw and may overwrite an initial foreign value. That
pre-existing behavior is not repaired or asserted to occur on actual boards.
Retry qualification is failed-init retry only, not live reset, NSS-to-EDMA
reverse handoff or global counter/state reinitialization.

Oracles
--------
All host fixture compiles require exit zero and empty compiler stdout/stderr. Candidate
suite and trace require exit zero and empty stderr. Suite accounting must
match exactly 36 cases / 4522 checks / node 65/65 / device 62/62 / DMA API
uses 70 / IRQ uses 8. Trace has one fewer mode-dispatch check.

Each of 14 semantic mutants must exit exactly 86, have empty stdout and emit
exactly its assigned single EDMA_OF016 marker on stderr. Wrong exit, extra
stdout, extra stderr and synthetic unrelated sanitizer diagnostics are four
rejected oracle-poison cases. Crashes, arbitrary nonzero exits and sanitizer
failures cannot satisfy a semantic mutant. Three actual old-001-015-source
runs (missing pdev, region failure, success/final) must fail specifically at
node-get-put-balance. Separate Clang ASan and UBSan canaries require positive
diagnostics and nonzero exits; they are not counted as semantic mutants.
Failures, commands, compiler streams and generated inputs are retained.

Residual scope
---------------
This is global EDMA-owned OF/device reference pairing, not a general lifetime
closure. External NSS/SSDK/PHY caches, asynchronous skb->dev/PTP, firmware
references, DMA idle/duplicate opaque epoch, common MDIO, EDMA v2 and target
compilation/runtime remain OPEN. The separate conditional P1 in outer
nss_dp_init failure rollback is not fixed by 016. The runner performs no
ring/IRQ tuning, forced DMA sweep, release/version/lock changes, staging or
commits. Parent package-release maintenance is a separate recorded action.
